# The relay's loopback gets whatever video number is free at boot; its name is
# fixed. Give Howdy a stable path, and keep the device root's alone: Howdy reads
# it as root, and a session process that could open it could watch the IR
# camera or, while the relay restarts, take the producer side and feed it
# frames. 70-uaccess tags every video4linux node for the seat user and
# 73-seat-late turns that tag into an ACL, so this runs in between.
# The link starts with "video" because OpenCV, which Howdy reads through, hands
# a path to FFmpeg first and FFmpeg takes it for a camera only by that prefix;
# OpenCV's V4L2 reader, which gets any other name, fails on loopback buffers.
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTR{name}=="HM1092 IR Camera", TAG-="uaccess", TAG-="seat", MODE="0600", GROUP="root", SYMLINK+="video-hm1092-ir"
